<title>DUBAI: Arab Banking Corp names new president/CEO.</title>
<headline>Arab Banking Corp names new president/CEO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arab Banking Corporation (ABC), one of the largest banks in the Arab World, on Wednesday appointed a new president and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Ghazi Abdul-Jawad, general manager of Gulf International Bank B.S.C since 1985, replaces Sheikh Ahmed Abdullatif, said the bank's board of directors in a statement issued in Manama.</p>
<p>The appointment takes effect on February 1, 1997, it added.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
